Imagine the JVM secretly generates something like
class StudentServiceProxy
implements StudentService {
    private InvocationHandler handler;
    public void addStudent(){

        handler.invoke(...);
    }
    public void deleteStudent(){

        handler.invoke(...);
    }
    public void updateStudent(){
        handler.invoke(...);
    }
}

You never wrote this class.

The JVM creates something equivalent in memory.

That's why it is called a Dynamic Proxy.